{
  "description": "Weather controller data. One global timeline gives each 30-90 minute segment a latent foulness value that moves by at most the volatility per segment. Each climate maps it through a fair-to-foul ladder of [TYPE, weight] pairs, so weights are long-run time shares. The weather can skip narrow rungs, but never changes severity by more than the climate's maxSeverityStep at once; the loader checks the weights between distant severities. Parameters are a number or [mild, severe], interpolated by how deep the latent is into its rung. A climate's wind only applies outdoors where the environment authors none, unless windBlend says otherwise. Bindings are ordered, the first match wins, and unbound points get no weather. Check time shares and spell lengths with ::117hd weather stats. See schemas/weather.schema.json.",
